{
  "assessment": "The change introduces `pipeline/ingest.py` to centralize raw record filtering, normalize types, and track drop reasons using an explicit `Accepted` collector. It replaces implicit or inline processing with strict validation paths for missing keys, invalid flags, unknown channels, and out-of-bounds values before appending kept records to a list. Because downstream aggregation relies on a populated sample window but this module's flag gate performs exact case-sensitive matching against lower-case constants, non-lowercase inputs are silently rejected; when enough (or all) are dropped, the resulting empty window triggers the reported `ZeroDivisionError` in `stats.summarise`.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "actual": "Records with upper/mixed-case flags fail the exact match check, increment `DROP_BAD_FLAG`, and are silently discarded. Downstream aggregation receives zero samples, causing `len(window.values)` to be empty and raising ZeroDivisionError at pipeline/stats.py:52.",
      "at": "pipeline/ingest.py, lines 63-66",
      "call": "python3 run.py data/samples.jsonl (input contains typical fleet flag casing like \"Good\" or \"DEGRADED\")",
      "defect": "Case-sensitive flag validation silently drops non-lowercase flags instead of normalizing them.",
      "expected": "Flag gate should normalize input case before validation (e.g., `.lower()`) so valid semantic flags pass the quality gate and populate the sample window."
    }
  ]
}
